00:32:50,970 --> 00:32:52,410
It's better to steam and barbecue it, right?

786
00:32:52,410 --> 00:32:53,480
You're right.

787
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:55,450
Prawns? Okay.

788
00:32:55,850 --> 00:32:56,950
Half a kilogram.

789
00:32:57,610 --> 00:32:59,880
Half a kilo? Good.

790
00:32:59,880 --> 00:33:00,920
(Adding tiger prawns)

791
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:02,090
Okay.

792
00:33:04,990 --> 00:33:08,790
In Vietnam, seafood is called "hải sản."

793
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:16,570
(Various types of fresh seafood are everywhere in the restaurant.)

794
00:33:18,430 --> 00:33:22,910
Da Nang is in central Vietnam, and thanks to its long coastline,

795
00:33:22,910 --> 00:33:27,480
you can enjoy fresh and diverse seafood on a budget.

796
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:33,150
(There are tons of colourful dishes crafted from fresh seafood.)

797
00:33:51,570 --> 00:33:55,610
At first, we became popular for selling food at low prices.

798
00:33:56,110 --> 00:34:00,210
More tourists visit in this season than in the winter.

799
00:34:00,210 --> 00:34:02,380
More customers from Hanoi visit us...

800
00:34:02,850 --> 00:34:05,050
in the summer.

801
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:09,520
There are all these people,

802
00:34:09,890 --> 00:34:11,750
and I don't see any Koreans.

803
00:34:14,260 --> 00:34:15,790
I ordered one that looked like a lobster.

804
00:34:15,790 --> 00:34:16,860
Okay.

805
00:34:17,230 --> 00:34:20,500
- That and 500g of prawns.
- Yes.

806
00:34:20,900 --> 00:34:23,070
And I heard their clams were good.

807
00:34:23,330 --> 00:34:25,000
Clams? Should we order those too?

808
00:34:25,300 --> 00:34:26,340
We should.

809
00:34:27,570 --> 00:34:28,600
Is this...

810
00:34:29,170 --> 00:34:30,970
like Garak Market in Korea?

811
00:34:31,710 --> 00:34:32,880
The night market in Jongro.

812
00:34:33,410 --> 00:34:34,540
You know Jongro is popular these days, right?

813
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:36,380
Oh, that's what it's like.

814
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:39,580
Okay.

815
00:34:42,790 --> 00:34:44,420
There's no English.

816
00:34:44,420 --> 00:34:45,490
Okay.

817
00:34:45,490 --> 00:34:49,190
(It's only in Vietnamese.)

818
00:34:49,890 --> 00:34:51,830
Seashell?

819
00:34:52,130 --> 00:34:54,260
(He describes it with his body.)

820
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:57,400
(Looking for a translator app)

821
00:34:58,200 --> 00:35:00,900
(Hyun Moo desperately wants clams.)

822
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:02,640
(Are you talking about this?)

823
00:35:03,310 --> 00:35:06,010
What is it? This is also in Vietnamese.

824
00:35:06,010 --> 00:35:08,480
(He showed Hyun Moo the Vietnamese word.)

825
00:35:08,680 --> 00:35:11,110
Scallop?

826
00:35:11,310 --> 00:35:12,480
- Scallop!
- Scallop?

827
00:35:12,620 --> 00:35:14,220
- Yes, scallop!
- Scallop!

828
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,490
- How did he know that word?
- Right?

829
00:35:16,850 --> 00:35:17,950
How did he know?

830
00:35:21,460 --> 00:35:23,060
Oh, man.

831
00:35:25,390 --> 00:35:31,430
(Tôm sú nuog mọi, Salt-grilled tiger prawn)

832
00:35:32,670 --> 00:35:33,800
Should we eat?

833
00:35:34,300 --> 00:35:35,510
I lost my appetite.

834
00:35:35,510 --> 00:35:36,510
(He worked out and lost his appetite.)

835
00:35:36,510 --> 00:35:38,210
Do we eat the whole thing?

836
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:40,510
Hold on. I'll take this off.

837
00:35:41,710 --> 00:35:43,550
- There you go.
- Just the head.

838
00:35:44,010 --> 00:35:45,080
And...

839
00:35:45,880 --> 00:35:47,150
dip it here.

840
00:35:52,620 --> 00:35:54,590
(Will it be good enough to bring back Hyun Moo's appetite?)

841
00:35:58,260 --> 00:35:59,300
It's good.

842
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:03,730
(He has no appetite, but he gives it a try.)

843
00:36:05,570 --> 00:36:07,140
(Carefully taking a bite)

844
00:36:09,710 --> 00:36:11,040
- It's good.
- It's so good.

845
00:36:11,040 --> 00:36:12,110
It's good.

846
00:36:19,080 --> 00:36:21,380
The prawns were grilled over charcoal,

847
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:24,390
so they have a smoky flavour.

848
00:36:24,390 --> 00:36:26,120
(Tiger prawn bursting with smoky flavour)

849
00:36:26,460 --> 00:36:27,890
The charcoal you're talking about is right there.

850
00:36:28,990 --> 00:36:30,990
Right. No wonder it tastes good.

851
00:36:31,430 --> 00:36:33,130
It has that flavour.

852
00:36:38,300 --> 00:36:42,840
(Grilling over an open flame for a smoky flavour)

853
00:36:48,010 --> 00:36:49,650
This is totally my style.

854
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:01,490
It's not even expensive.

855
00:37:14,070 --> 00:37:15,770
Look at the flesh.

856
00:37:19,140 --> 00:37:21,580
I'm sweating so much because of that Vietnamese Lee Kang In.

857
00:37:21,580 --> 00:37:22,850
I'm still sweating.

858
00:37:23,310 --> 00:37:24,780
It's so hot.

859
00:37:25,150 --> 00:37:26,720
I can't stop sweating.

860
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:29,250
It's so hot.

861
00:37:29,520 --> 00:37:30,850
I can't stop sweating.

862
00:37:34,390 --> 00:37:36,760
(Rau muống xào, Stir-fried water spinach)

863
00:37:39,960 --> 00:37:40,960
Scallop.

864
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:43,300
(Sò điệp nướng, Grilled scallops)

865
00:37:51,610 --> 00:37:53,880
The scallop was cooked so well. What is this?

866
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:55,340
It's really good.

867
00:37:57,950 --> 00:37:59,180
(A flavour that wakes you up)

868
00:37:59,180 --> 00:38:01,180
It's amazing, isn't it?

869
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:02,450
This is really good.

870
00:38:04,020 --> 00:38:05,150
This...

871
00:38:06,690 --> 00:38:09,260
You have to put the whole thing in your mouth at once.

872
00:38:11,890 --> 00:38:13,030
Peanuts.

873
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:16,800
I think it has peanuts, a spicy sauce,

874
00:38:17,370 --> 00:38:18,700
cheongyang pepper,

875
00:38:19,200 --> 00:38:21,040
and garlic flakes.

876
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:22,570
Who wouldn't like this?

877
00:38:26,010 --> 00:38:28,280
They're really good with combinations.

878
00:38:30,410 --> 00:38:31,680
It tastes really good.

879
00:38:33,180 --> 00:38:35,820
The scallops are amazing.

880
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:38,390
This one.

881
00:38:46,730 --> 00:38:49,500
Vietnamese food really suits Korean tastes.

882
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:51,100
Isn't that right?

883
00:38:54,140 --> 00:38:55,910
(We have some broth!)

884
00:38:58,610 --> 00:39:01,180
(Nghêu hấp, Steamed clams)

885
00:39:04,850 --> 00:39:06,050
This is amazing.

886
00:39:06,720 --> 00:39:07,820
Is this like...

887
00:39:08,420 --> 00:39:10,220
mussel soup?

888
00:39:14,790 --> 00:39:16,290
No. It's like clam soup.

889
00:39:17,060 --> 00:39:18,290
Clear clam soup.

890
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:22,500
This is a familiar taste.

891
00:39:22,630 --> 00:39:24,230
- One you have with alcohol.
- It's a familiar taste.

892
00:39:24,900 --> 00:39:29,070
(Steamed clams with a flavour similar to clam soup)

893
00:39:29,910 --> 00:39:31,010
It's a taste we know.

894
00:39:31,410 --> 00:39:32,710
Right? It's a familiar taste.

895
00:39:33,310 --> 00:39:34,440
It would be perfect with soju.

896
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:36,380
It's similar to the Korean dish.

897
00:39:36,810 --> 00:39:38,580
The difference...

898
00:39:38,580 --> 00:39:40,380
is that the broth has a cilantro flavour.

899
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:42,150
- Just a bit.
- Yes.

900
00:39:42,150 --> 00:39:43,690
But it doesn't taste strange.

901
00:39:43,950 --> 00:39:44,950
It's still nice, isn't it?

902
00:39:44,950 --> 00:39:45,960
It's tasty.

903
00:39:46,590 --> 00:39:47,990
The main dish isn't here yet.

904
00:39:48,160 --> 00:39:49,230
You're right.

905
00:39:49,890 --> 00:39:51,860
I'm almost mad that I'm getting full.

906
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,570
Do you eat a lot of food when you drink?

907
00:39:57,030 --> 00:39:58,230
It depends.

908
00:39:59,070 --> 00:40:00,570
I usually eat more.

909
00:40:01,270 --> 00:40:03,970
It's Friday night, but not many people...

910
00:40:04,510 --> 00:40:06,140
are drinking beer.

911
00:40:06,740 --> 00:40:08,510
I just looked around to see what they're eating.

912
00:40:08,510 --> 00:40:09,950
They drink Coke more.

913
00:40:10,050 --> 00:40:12,280
It feels like Vietnamese people don't drink so much.

914
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:13,750
- That's right.
- It's an atmosphere...

915
00:40:13,750 --> 00:40:15,350
that definitely calls for alcohol, but...

916
00:40:15,350 --> 00:40:16,490
(A restaurant the locals come to have a late dinner)

917
00:40:16,750 --> 00:40:19,220
The Gen Z people in Korea also don't drink so much.

918
00:40:19,660 --> 00:40:23,130
I heard the younger generation don't like being tipsy.

919
00:40:23,360 --> 00:40:25,490
Really? I envy them so much.

920
00:40:26,230 --> 00:40:28,700
I get like this after two glasses.

921
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:31,470
- That's good.
- I doze off.

922
00:40:32,130 --> 00:40:33,670
You won the Grand Award at the Entertainment Awards.

923
00:40:33,670 --> 00:40:35,200
It's such a happy day.

924
00:40:35,340 --> 00:40:36,570
You still wouldn't drink?

925
00:40:36,640 --> 00:40:40,110
On days like that, people make you drink.

926
00:40:40,840 --> 00:40:43,280
I drink once or twice...

927
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:44,510
and throw away the third.

928
00:40:44,510 --> 00:40:45,710
Then I act like I'm drunk.

929
00:40:45,750 --> 00:40:47,080
Really?

930
00:40:49,850 --> 00:40:51,450
Then you go home, right?

931
00:40:51,450 --> 00:40:52,690
(Acting like he's drunk)

932
00:40:52,860 --> 00:40:54,920
Manager, please take Hyun Moo home.

933
00:40:55,190 --> 00:40:57,060
I can stay.

934
00:40:57,060 --> 00:40:58,730
Give me a glass.

935
00:40:59,230 --> 00:41:01,360
I do that as well.

936
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:03,100
I do the same thing.

937
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:04,630
I do that at gatherings.

938
00:41:05,940 --> 00:41:07,700
And when the door shuts...

939
00:41:07,700 --> 00:41:08,770
(When the door shuts)

940
00:41:08,770 --> 00:41:10,370
- That's right.
- Let's go, Manager.

941
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:13,410
That's right.

942
00:41:13,410 --> 00:41:15,340
I act so well.

943
00:41:15,340 --> 00:41:16,850
I'm good at doing this.

944
00:41:16,850 --> 00:41:19,720
(Hyun Moo is an expert at acting drunk.)

945
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:23,320
- Okay!
- No way!

946
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:24,320
Okay.

947
00:41:24,950 --> 00:41:26,920
Crayfish! Lobster.

948
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:30,130
This is really...

949
00:41:30,130 --> 00:41:31,690
(Tôm hùm đất nướng bơ, Butter-grilled crayfish)

950
00:41:31,690 --> 00:41:32,830
This is their signature dish.

951
00:41:32,830 --> 00:41:34,130
This is crazy.

952
00:41:40,770 --> 00:41:42,840
Goodness. Look at how plump it is.

953
00:41:48,080 --> 00:41:49,810
See if you can taste a difference from regular lobster.

954
00:41:49,810 --> 00:41:50,810
Okay.

955
00:42:01,360 --> 00:42:02,560
It's chewy.

956
00:42:02,560 --> 00:42:04,030
(It has a chewy texture.)

957
00:42:04,030 --> 00:42:05,160
It's really good.

958
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:06,660
The way I see it,

959
00:42:07,230 --> 00:42:08,560
it would have been...

960
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,170
really vicious when it was in the sea.

961
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:19,810
Crayfish is also considered a luxury ingredient in Vietnam.

962
00:42:20,040 --> 00:42:26,080
This seafood is very popular in Vietnam...

963
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:32,960
because you can really taste its freshness and quality.

964
00:42:34,090 --> 00:42:39,030
It can be enjoyed in many different ways,

965
00:42:39,030 --> 00:42:43,130
including grilled, steamed, fried, and stir-fried.

966
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:46,800
What's that?

967
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:48,340
- What's going on?
- What kind of show is this?

968
00:42:48,340 --> 00:42:49,370
Who is she?

969
00:42:49,910 --> 00:42:51,910
(Presenter and local coordinator...)

970
00:42:51,910 --> 00:42:53,910
(responsible for sharing local culture and information)

971
00:42:53,910 --> 00:42:55,680
I thought this was a different show.

972
00:42:56,880 --> 00:42:58,810
We're only supporting actors.

973
00:42:59,950 --> 00:43:01,420
We're just reenactment actors.

974
00:43:01,420 --> 00:43:02,420
In the background.

975
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:03,420
Hello.

976
00:43:07,090 --> 00:43:08,620
While filming this,

977
00:43:09,060 --> 00:43:10,690
there's something I'm worried about.

978
00:43:10,990 --> 00:43:14,000
I only had fun without thinking about the show.

979
00:43:14,360 --> 00:43:15,530
That would make this show a big hit.

980
00:43:15,530 --> 00:43:16,530
Really?

981
00:43:16,900 --> 00:43:19,570
If the viewers know what we do for the show,

982
00:43:19,570 --> 00:43:21,040
they won't watch it then.

983
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:23,970
I feel like I'm just having fun, forgetting the camera is there.

984
00:43:23,970 --> 00:43:25,470
I'm not even wearing underwear.

985
00:43:26,110 --> 00:43:28,010
- So...
- I'm not wearing my underwear.

986
00:43:28,280 --> 00:43:31,710
We're both over 40...

987
00:43:31,710 --> 00:43:33,220
I'm soon turning 50.

988
00:43:35,620 --> 00:43:38,250
And this place itself is amazing.

989
00:43:38,850 --> 00:43:40,660
I've been abroad for many shows,

990
00:43:41,590 --> 00:43:44,490
but every famous place was filled with Korean people.

991
00:43:45,130 --> 00:43:46,400
It felt like we were always behind.

992
00:43:46,400 --> 00:43:47,560
(The kind of trip where he always felt like he was a step behind)

993
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:50,270
It's not because we're celebrities.

994
00:43:50,630 --> 00:43:52,030
- You don't have to be a celebrity.
- You don't have to be one.

995
00:43:52,030 --> 00:43:54,640
When Korean people go abroad,

996
00:43:54,640 --> 00:43:56,240
they don't like places with many Koreans.

997
00:43:56,310 --> 00:43:59,510
We're not trying to see or experience amazing things.

998
00:44:00,080 --> 00:44:01,910
We're just putting ourselves in an environment...

999
00:44:01,910 --> 00:44:03,350
that's completely different from Korea.

1000
00:44:03,850 --> 00:44:05,180
That heals you.

1001
00:44:05,180 --> 00:44:06,350
(That's when the real healing begins.)

1002
00:44:06,350 --> 00:44:07,980
I also like this because it's simple.

1003
00:44:08,650 --> 00:44:10,790
We didn't do anything big.

1004
00:44:10,890 --> 00:44:13,990
- So, when I was at the airport, - Yes.

1005
00:44:15,490 --> 00:44:17,190
- I booked a train ticket.
- What?

1006
00:44:17,190 --> 00:44:18,930
- I booked a train ticket.
- A train?

1007
00:44:19,530 --> 00:44:21,160
- We have to do this as we planned.
- Okay.

1008
00:44:21,930 --> 00:44:23,030
Because...

1009
00:44:23,600 --> 00:44:25,970
it was the only thing I had in mind in Korea.

1010
00:44:28,540 --> 00:44:29,910
Vietnam's Gyeongju.

1011
00:44:30,170 --> 00:44:32,840
That's nice. Gyeongju is nice.

1012
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:34,410
It's nice.

1013
00:44:34,710 --> 00:44:36,610
But it takes four hours to get there.

1014
00:44:36,610 --> 00:44:38,510
So we need to set our minds to it.

1015
00:44:38,510 --> 00:44:39,620
It's a long trip.

1016
00:44:40,050 --> 00:44:41,850
That's why I booked the train tickets...

1017
00:44:41,850 --> 00:44:43,220
when I arrived at the airport.

1018
00:44:43,220 --> 00:44:44,650
- It's for tomorrow morning.
- Really?

1019
00:44:44,650 --> 00:44:46,220
- Tomorrow morning's train?
- Yes.

1020
00:44:46,220 --> 00:44:48,720
Travelling by train abroad is really romantic.

1021
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:49,730
It is romantic.

1022
00:44:50,260 --> 00:44:51,660
I like that.

1023
00:44:52,960 --> 00:44:54,500
Then today's the last night at our accommodation.

1024
00:44:54,860 --> 00:44:55,860
That's right.

1025
00:44:56,530 --> 00:44:58,870
- I want to go swimming then.
- You can go swimming.

1026
00:44:58,870 --> 00:44:59,940
I'll swim then.

1027
00:45:00,070 --> 00:45:01,570
You can enjoy your time.

1028
00:45:02,100 --> 00:45:03,110
Okay.

1029
00:45:03,110 --> 00:45:04,440
Nice. Let's go.

1030
00:45:05,210 --> 00:45:06,480
(Total: approximately 121 dollars)

1031
00:45:06,480 --> 00:45:09,080
- Today was so amazing.
- Let's go.

1032
00:45:09,380 --> 00:45:10,810
- Thank you for the food.
- I'm so full.

1033
00:45:10,810 --> 00:45:11,880
It's so nice.

1034
00:45:15,520 --> 00:45:19,050
(It's their last night in Da Nang. It's too good to waste on sleep.)

1035
00:45:20,520 --> 00:45:22,490
(Screaming)

1036
00:45:24,490 --> 00:45:26,230
(Joon enjoys a swim in the pool at their accommodation.)

1037
00:45:26,230 --> 00:45:27,230
This is nice.

1038
00:45:27,830 --> 00:45:29,830
- Is it warm?
- It's nice. It's cool.

1039
00:45:33,170 --> 00:45:34,440
(He dips himself in cool water...)

1040
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:35,440
Nice.

1041
00:45:35,440 --> 00:45:39,410
(and washes away the fatigue from the day.)

1042
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,180
Nice.

1043
00:45:42,710 --> 00:45:45,550
- The water is refreshing.
- You have amazing shoulders.

1044
00:45:45,550 --> 00:45:46,550
Really?

1045
00:45:46,780 --> 00:45:48,350
(Should I show off my shoulders a bit?)

1046
00:46:03,670 --> 00:46:05,370
I want to take all my clothes off and have fun.

1047
00:46:05,630 --> 00:46:06,670
Take it off.

1048
00:46:08,900 --> 00:46:10,810
("This is Hyunmoo Road" is just as good as "Solo's Inferno.")

1049
00:46:10,810 --> 00:46:12,940
Look at those shoulders and back muscles.

1050
00:46:13,780 --> 00:46:15,380
But it's so...

1051
00:46:15,610 --> 00:46:18,010
